  "description": "Write Minecraft Fabric mods in C# instead of Java. Reference this package, write your mod logic using the CSCraft API, then run dotnet build — the transpiler converts your C# to Java, generates recipe JSON files automatically, and optionally runs Gradle to produce a ready-to-install .jar.\n\nSupports: blocks (with mining categories and tool levels), items, armor, tools, food, events, commands, recipes (shaped, shapeless, smelting, blasting, smoking, campfire, stonecutting), auto-generated models/blockstates/lang/tag files, custom textures and sounds, entity tags, status effects, enchantments, particles, sounds, advancements, loot tables, villager trades, game rules, and more. JAR auto-copies to your project folder.\n\nTarget: Minecraft 1.21.1 · Fabric API 0.116.9+1.21.1 · Java 21",
